      "content": "{\"classifications\":{\"42\":\"1\",\"50\":\"0\",\"57\":\"1\",\"89\":\"1\",\"133\":\"0\",\"157\":\"0\",\"189\":\"1\",\"214\":\"0\",\"240\":\"0\",\"299\":\"1\",\"453\":\"0\",\"490\":\"0\",\"597\":\"0\",\"630\":\"0\",\"656\":\"0\",\"714\":\"1\",\"721\":\"0\",\"744\":\"1\",\"773\":\"1\",\"794\":\"1\",\"805\":\"0\",\"817\":\"1\",\"871\":\"1\",\"873\":\"1\",\"918\":\"0\",\"964\":\"0\",\"967\":\"0\",\"1021\":\"0\",\"1043\":\"1\",\"1060\":\"1\",\"1086\":\"1\",\"1118\":\"0\",\"1139\":\"0\",\"1155\":\"1\",\"1177\":\"0\",\"1230\":\"1\",\"1257\":\"1\",\"1313\":\"0\",\"1320\":\"1\",\"1325\":\"0\",\"1610\":\"0\",\"1736\":\"1\",\"1747\":\"1\",\"1749\":\"1\",\"1827\":\"1\",\"1862\":\"1\",\"1897\":\"0\",\"1927\":\"1\",\"1957\":\"0\",\"2003\":\"0\",\"2026\":\"1\",\"2143\":\"0\",\"2318\":\"1\",\"2335\":\"1\",\"2368\":\"1\",\"2382\":\"1\",\"2627\":\"1\",\"2675\":\"1\",\"2697\":\"1\",\"2807\":\"1\",\"2827\":\"0\",\"2869\":\"0\",\"2895\":\"1\",\"3038\":\"0\",\"3047\":\"1\",\"3143\":\"1\",\"3149\":\"1\",\"3201\":\"1\",\"3252\":\"1\",\"3271\":\"1\",\"3477\":\"1\",\"3482\":\"0\",\"3501\":\"0\",\"3534\":\"0\",\"3560\":\"0\",\"3577\":\"1\",\"3659\":\"0\",\"3687\":\"0\",\"3729\":\"1\",\"3744\":\"1\",\"3817\":\"0\",\"3845\":\"1\",\"3914\":\"0\",\"3950\":\"1\",\"4022\":\"1\",\"4122\":\"1\",\"4124\":\"0\",\"4184\":\"1\",\"4207\":\"1\",\"4208\":\"1\",\"4295\":\"1\",\"4328\":\"1\",\"4344\":\"1\",\"4403\":\"1\",\"4508\":\"1\",\"4531\":\"1\",\"4585\":\"1\",\"4677\":\"0\",\"4771\":\"1\",\"4774\":\"1\"},\"codebook\":{\"definition\":\"Credit-claiming occurs when a senator presents themself, alone or with colleagues, as having materially helped produce, secure, protect, advance, or deliver a policy, program, funding award, government action, or constituent benefit.\",\"clarification\":\"Classify a release as credit-claiming when it explicitly attributes an accomplishment or concrete effort to the senator. This includes saying that the senator authored, introduced, secured, obtained, delivered, helped pass, successfully pushed for, negotiated, or used oversight to achieve a result. It also includes claiming a substantive role in a government decision or grant, even if other officials or legislators shared the effort. Legislative sponsorship and successful amendments count when the release frames them as the senator's work or achievement.\",\"positive_examples\":[{\"text\":\"Sen. Talent announces that the Senate approved his request for $1.5 million for the University of Missouri Health Sciences Research and Education Facility.\",\"explanation\":\"This explicitly attributes the appropriated funding to Talent's request, directly claiming credit for obtaining a local benefit.\"},{\"text\":\"Senator Durbin states that he helped secure an expedited environmental review and facilitated the return of the South Suburban Airport project to the national priority list for federal funding.\",\"explanation\":\"Durbin identifies specific actions he took and connects them to advancement of the airport project.\"},{\"text\":\"Sen. Dorgan says he authored legislation, signed into law, that created Bismarck State College's National Center designation.\",\"explanation\":\"The senator claims authorship of the enacted law that enabled the announced designation.\"}],\"negative_clarification\":\"Do not classify a release as credit-claiming when it merely states a policy view, criticizes or praises another official, announces a government decision or grant without claiming a role in obtaining it, honors a person or group, or describes a planned future action. A vote or general support statement alone is not enough unless it is framed as the senator's accomplishment in delivering a concrete outcome.\",\"negative_examples\":[{\"text\":\"Sen. Reid criticizes the Bush Administration's response to global warming and urges it to show leadership.\",\"explanation\":\"This is position-taking and criticism of the administration; Reid does not claim to have delivered a policy result.\"},{\"text\":\"Sens. Dodd and Lieberman announce a Department of Transportation grant for Bradley International Airport.\",\"explanation\":\"The release reports the grant and its expected benefits but does not say either senator secured, requested, or otherwise caused the award.\"},{\"text\":\"Sen. Ensign comments after the Senate confirms Michael Chertoff as Homeland Security Secretary and says he looks forward to working with him.\",\"explanation\":\"The senator offers an evaluation of the nominee and a future-oriented statement, not a claim of personal accomplishment.\"}]}}",
